+\section{Result at a glance}
+
+The proposal adds one generic module and two contender-specific modules:
+
+\begin{center}
+\small
+\begin{tabular}{P{0.38\textwidth}P{0.52\textwidth}}
+\toprule
+File & Role\\
+\midrule
+\code{TransfiniteHyper\allowbreak Reflection.lean} & Hyperlifts, lift splicing,
+W-tree iteration, preservation and strictness theorems.\\
+\code{Contender20.lean} & The two autonomous schedules, the finite seed lift,
+the W-rank lift, \(F_{20}\), and \code{contender\_20}.\\
+\code{Comparison20.lean} & The pointwise comparison chain,
+\code{contender\_19\_lt\_contender\_20}, and the program-value bound.\\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{center}
+
+The headline definition is short:
+
+\begin{lstlisting}
+def family19 (n : Nat) : Nat := F19 (F19 n)
+
+def seedLift20 (n : Nat) : TransformerLift :=
+  diagonalLift (schedule20 n) (family19 n + 1)
+
+def lift20 (n : Nat) : TransformerLift :=
+  treeDiagonalLift (schedule20 n) (rankTree20 n) (seedLift20 n)
+
+def F20 (n : Nat) : Nat :=
+  lift20 n lTransformer seedFamily20 n n
+
+def contender_20 : Nat := F20 (F20 42)
+\end{lstlisting}
+
+The proof is deliberately factored into three strict inequalities:
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:chain}
+\underbrace{\mathrm{family19}(n)}_{F_{19}(F_{19}(n))}
+<\underbrace{L(\mathrm{seed}_{20})}_{\text{one large-Veblen reflection}}
+<\underbrace{D_n(L)(\mathrm{seed}_{20})}_{\text{finite-rank seed lift}}
+<\underbrace{W_n(D_n)(L)(\mathrm{seed}_{20})}_{F_{20}(n)}.
+\end{equation}
+Here \(L\) is the existing large-Veblen reflector, \(D_n\) is a diagonal lift
+of rank \(\mathrm{family19}(n)+1\), and \(W_n\) is the new W-tree rank closure.
+Each arrow is witnessed by an existing or newly proved strict-inflation
+property; no appeal is made to an informal ordinal estimate.
+
+\paragraph{Formal status.}
